{
  "$comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the fidelity fixtures. scripts/gen-fixtures.py turns each case's",
    "content blocks into Anthropic-dialect message dicts, calls upstream CliffCompaction compact()",
    "with keep_recent forced to 0 so every turn is summarised, and writes the resulting summary text",
    "to test/fixtures/expected.json. test/cliff.test.ts turns the same case into SummaryUnit values,",
    "renders them with src/cliff.ts, and compares the assembled text byte for byte.",
    "",
    "keep_recent is not represented here: pi owns the cut, so the harness compacts everything and",
    "compares only the summarised region. The leading human and system messages are upstream's verbatim",
    "head and are excluded from the comparison, which is what renderSummary's separate headSection is for.",
    "",
    "A text value is either a string or {\"$repeat\": [\"X\", 3000]}, which both readers expand the same way,",
    "so long strings stay readable in this file. Escape sequences are JSON's own, so a control character",
    "here is the real character on both sides.",
    "",
    "config is what upstream compacts with. renderConfig, when present, is what test/cliff.test.ts",
    "renders with, and profile (default \"manual\") is the profile it renders under: the two overflow",
    "cases pin that a configured policy plus the overflow profile equals the lean policy upstream ran."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "basic_session_folds_every_turn",
      "mirrors": "tests/test_cliff.py::test_basic_structure_anthropic",
      "note": "Upstream's a_session layout: a task, then alternating fat and thin tool results.",
      "config": {},
      "messages": [
        {
          "role": "human",
          "blocks": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Fix the failing test in repo X." }]
        },
        {
          "role": "assistant",
          "blocks": [
            { "type": "text", "text": "Step 0: I will inspect module 0 to find the bug." },
            {
              "type": "toolCall",
              "id": "tu_0",
              "name": "bash",
              "args": { "command": "pytest tests/test_0.py -x" }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "toolResult",
          "toolUseId": "tu_0",
          "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": { "$repeat": ["X", 3000] } }]
        },
        {
          "role": "assistant",
          "blocks": [
            { "type": "text", "text": "Step 1: I will inspect module 1 to find the bug." },
            {
              "type": "toolCall",
              "id": "tu_1",
              "name": "bash",
              "args": { "command": "pytest tests/test_1.py -x" }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "toolResult",
          "toolUseId": "tu_1",
          "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "test_1 passed (short output)" }]
        },
        {
          "role": "assistant",
          "blocks": [
            { "type": "text", "text": "Step 2: I will inspect module 2 to find the bug." },
            {
              "type": "toolCall",
              "id": "tu_2",
              "name": "bash",
              "args": { "command": "pytest tests/test_2.py -x" }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "toolResult",
          "toolUseId": "tu_2",
          "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": { "$repeat": ["X", 3000] } }]
        },
        {
          "role": "assistant",
          "blocks": [
            { "type": "text", "text": "Step 3: I will inspect module 3 to find the bug." },
            {
              "type": "toolCall",
              "id": "tu_3",
              "name": "bash",
              "args": { "command": "pytest tests/test_3.py -x" }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "toolResult",
          "toolUseId": "tu_3",
          "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "test_3 passed (short output)" }]
        }
      ]
    },
