      "mirrors": "src/cliffcompaction/hashing.py::canonical_json",
      "note": "Keys are zero-padded so sorted order is the order below. Integral values are integers on both sides and fractional ones take Python's fixed or exponent form. A float literal that happens to be integral, such as 3.0, 9007199254740991.5 or 1.0e+16, is the one class this port cannot render the upstream way, so no case here uses one. n12 is the widest literal that stays fractional on both sides.",
